 comfort Flexible scheduling options Up to 12 free make-up lessons per membership year A positive learning environment And much more! If structured progression and consistent teaching matter to you, our swim school in Oakville offers a clear path forward. Have questions? Get in touch with our team by calling us at (289) 806-3919 to learn more. Swim Programs for Every Age and Skill Level Proper placement determines long-term success. Every swimmer gets a swim skills assessment before beginning formal lessons so instructors can identify readiness, coordination level, and water comfort. That evaluation ensures swimmers are introduced to the right starting point rather than being placed too high or too low. From there, infant swim lessons introduce early water familiarity through guided interaction, while older swimmers progress through structured levels designed to match developmental stages. A Family-Focused Swim School Serving Oakville Throughout Oakville and nearby communities such as Mississauga and Milton, our swim lessons in Oakville emphasize milestone-based advancement. We are proud to be the Winner of the 2026 Canadian Choice Award for Best Swim Instructors – Oakville, a recognition that reflects the professionalism, consistency, and instructional quality local families experience in our programs. This reinforces the trust families place in our team to deliver structured lessons that support steady skill development. Our Commitment to Water Safety in the Oakville Community Confidence in the water depends on awareness as much as movement. Within our kids’ swim school in Oakville, swimmers practice safe entry and exit techniques, breath control, and spatial awareness in shared aquatic environments. Instruction integrates safety habits into every level, reinforcing caution alongside coordination. FAQs About Our Swim School in Oakville Parents often have questions about when to begin, how lessons are structured, and what progress typically looks like from week to week. The answers below provide helpful guidance as you plan your child’s swim journey. What age can my child start at Goldfish Swim School? Enrollment begins at four months. As swimmers grow, preschool swim lessons strengthen coordination and floating control in structured stages. How often do families typically attend swim lessons? Weekly attendance supports skill retention and steady development across levels. What should my child bring to swim class? Swimmers should bring a swimsuit, towel, and reusable swim diapers if needed. Goggles may be used for comfort. How long does it typically take for kids to learn basic swim skills? Development varies based on readiness and consistency. Programs for a swim school for babies in Oakville focus on early familiarity before advancing toward stronger foundational ability. What water safety skills should children learn first? Floating stability, controlled entry and exit techniques, breath management, and awareness in active pool environments are introduced first. Winner of the 2026 Canadian Choice Award for Best Swim Instructors – Oakville! Discover Goldfish and give your kids the courage to dive in today! Contact us at (289) 806-3919 to get started. Meet Our Team Jackie O'Rourke Owner --> Derek O'Rourke Owner --> Andrew Anzil General Manager --> Roxy Hercules Aquatic Manager --> Peju Garraway Member Service Coordinator --> Clayton Marshall Junior Manager --> Jadin Dodd-Robyn Marketing Manager --> View All Teammates Now Hiring Not ready to book? Contact us Get Your Free Trial! Why Goldfish? Confidence-building curriculum Flexible class times Shiver-free, 90-degree pool Safety skills, socialization & fun Testimonials \"We’ve been attending here for about a year and it is great. The staff is kinda and knowledgeable and the kids love it!\" Nicole S. August 2, 2026 \"Just wanted to say this is really the first swim class my almost 6 year old has actually wanted to go to. He has done...\" Vgg August 7, 2026 \"Trial class went we